Subject: [PATCH 1/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 1;
 built on a35fd4bce with the ten patches of series 4 applied): A DEBT CHECKER
 READS NO CLOCK, AND NO ZONE OF THE MACHINE (Review 79, the second reader's
 row 20, its second and third parts; the failure main saw once, M10). The
 harvest checker timed its own run and printed the time at the end of its
 first line. When the checker fails, its gate gives that line back as its
 answer, so a failing harvest gate gave another answer at every run. A test of
 the first series' lock asks each debt gate three times and compares; it
 failed once on main's machine and said the day had moved the gate. It was the
 duration: reproduced by the seat, ten failures of ten where the harvest gate
 fails, none where it passes, with worktrees added and removed or without. And
 the checker turned a commit's time into a day in the zone of the machine it
 runs on, so a seat's item could be aged on one machine and not on another, on
 the same commit. THE MEND: the run is not timed, and no line of the report
 carries a duration; a commit's time is turned into a day in UTC. The lock's
 test that no gate and no checker reads the wall clock now refuses a duration
 too, and a call that makes a date of a time without naming its zone; until
 now it let a duration be timed, with a dated note of why that changes. The
 test of the day asks once more with the first day, and says so where a gate
 gives two answers with the day unchanged. What it does not reach: the passing
 sentence of the harvest gate names how far each seat's branch is past its pin
 in the clone, and a fetch between two runs moves it; that is the clone and
 not the commit, and is as it was. The lock: three tests added to
 tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py. On the commit before, two
 fail: the checker's line ends with how long it ran, and a note made at half
 past eleven at night is aged where the machine's zone is behind and not where
 it is ahead. The third reads this repository and passes wherever no debt gate
 fails. Tested against planted errors; reproduced; computed once. 0 of 19.

